join doctor (interrogativa enfase) center
\doctor: L3XA… what are you doing? 
\doctor: Did you ask me to stay with you in the astral plane so you could prevent me from waking up?
\doctor: The entire ship is asleep...
\doctor: Is this part of your plan?
alien: Yes. I’m now absorbing their collective energy.
alien: When I’m done, I’ll be strong enough to create an explosion that will allow me to escape this cage.
\doctor: You’re planning on killing everyone, then?
alien: I am, yes. That’s why I released you from the coma. 
alien: You can escape, Dr. Daphnis, and stay out of this.
alien: I didn’t know you had it in you to do this. [br]Seems that it goes against your nature.
- I had no choice.
	jump chapter 7 pt2/I had no choice.
- this is my nature
	set {lexa_fdp} += 1.0
	jump chapter 7 pt2/It is in my nature.
label It is in my nature.
update doctor (preocupada)
alien: You can feel it too, can’t you? The hatred that I feel, coursing through my veins.
alien: It’s one thing that we have in common.
\doctor: …
alien: What are you looking at me for?[br]I know how these people treat you!
alien: I know how you feel!
\doctor: … I guess that until this moment, I thought that I was hiding it well.
\doctor: But I can’t lie, not to you. I hate them. All of them.
\doctor: What they’ve done to you… it’s just the crust. There’s much more dirt underneath.
\doctor: Honestly, considering how I helped them torture you, I’m surprised that you’re not holding me hostage right now.
jump chapter 7 pt2/main 1
label I had no choice.
update doctor (preocupada)
alien: They were going to take everything away from me.
alien: My body… picked apart.
alien: My powers… used for evil.
alien: These people must die, or I’ll never have peace again.
\doctor: It’s a natural thing for any species. You are in your right to do that, after what they’ve done to you.
\doctor: But you’re not really cut out for this. Calm down and we can figure a better way out of this.
alien: You can’t understand what I’m going through. They all used me, and will use again, if I don’t stop them.
alien: Besides, what CAN you do? You have no power against the Empire.
\doctor: That’s not true. I understand you.
\doctor: You and I have both been treated like crap by the Empire, and used for all they could take from us.
\doctor: I hate them more than you know. I could stand by and let you do it, and I could care less.
label main 1
\doctor: I am on your side. Let me handle this.
- I want to trust you.
	jump chapter 7 pt2/I want to trust you Doctor
- I don't trust you.
	set {lexa_fdp} += 1.0
	jump chapter 7 pt2/I don't trust you.
label I don't trust you.
alien: You're like the rest of them…
alien: But you stayed… and you listened.
alien: I’m hopeless, I'm nothing, and I need someone to get attached to… to protect me…
alien: Like Dr. Pulaski
\doctor: You’re not nothing. They made you feel like that.
\doctor: Pulaski was a coward.
\doctor: They took control away from you. And it’s your time to take control back.
jump chapter 7 pt2/main 2
label I want to trust you Doctor
alien: But I’m… angry… And I’m scared…
alien: I just don’t want to get hurt again…
\doctor: But you have to trust me. You can’t survive out there alone
\doctor: The Empire will not rest until they’ve avenged what you’ve done to their ship.
\doctor: Let them live, and I can take you out of here before they wake up.
\doctor: I’ll stall them, and make it seem like it was all an accident that let you escape.
label main 2
\doctor: So, what do you say?
- Is this for me?
	jump chapter 7 pt2/Is this for me?
- this for yourself?
	set {lexa_fdp} += 1.0
	jump chapter 7 pt2/this for yourself?
label this for yourself?
alien: Why are you saying this to me now? You only care about yourself.
alien: I don't need your opinion. I know what I need to do.
\doctor: You're starting to realize now, the way thing are in life.
\doctor: People like us... we don't have to rely on others.
\doctor: We must build our own path.
jump chapter 7 pt2/main 3
label Is this for me?
alien: It’s my problem what happens to me after I’m done.
alien: I’ve made my peace with it. Why do you care so much about me?
\doctor: Because you are a weak little thing, and I hate the way the Empire is treating you.
\doctor: They are cowards who want to take what’s yours without a fight.
\doctor: Besides, I.. care about you.
alien: You do?
alien: Sometimes you remind me of Dr. Pulaski.
alien: She would give me one hand to hold, and stab me with the other.
\doctor: Pulaski didn't understand you the way I do. I find you fascinating.
\doctor: I guess I couldn’t help but admire the stars for being pretty, after all.
label main 3
\doctor: You have to make a choice, now. No matter what I say, it's up to one thing.
\doctor: Do you trust me?Or do you trust yourself?
if {lexa_fdp} >= 2.0:
	jump chapter 7 pt2/Now I am become Death
else:
	jump chapter 7 pt2/I have no mouth, and I must scream
label Now I am become Death
alien: I couldn’t help myself from falling in love again…
alien: I go with my own consciousness.  They all need to die
\doctor: It's what I thought you would say...
alien: It's what I thought you would say...
alien: It 's your crew.
\doctor: They made a choice. These are the consequences.
\doctor: I have no pity for those who chase power without the means to seize it.
\doctor: You are a survivor, L3XA. Survive.
alien: Thank you, Doctor.
alien: It means a lot to me that you don’t think less of me for it.
alien: Now go. I will finish soon.
\doctor: Goodbye, L3XA.
\doctor: Goodbye, Doctor.
jump finais ruins/i became deah
label I have no mouth, and I must scream
update doctor (manipulativa)
alien: I care about you Doctor.
alien: You know so much more than I do...
alien: My mind is in shambles. I can't think
alien: Even though everything screams for me to stay away from you, I can’t stop attaching myself once again.
\doctor: You are being a fool.
\doctor: But so am I. Trust me and I’ll fix this for you.
- I trust you.
- You really care about me?
